# Root-level monorepo .gitignore.
# Each subproject (app/, frontend/, backend/) may have its own .gitignore for
# specifics. This file covers things that should never be committed regardless
# of location.

# Dependencies (per-project node_modules)
**/node_modules/

# Build outputs
**/dist/
**/release/
**/.astro/
app/dist/
app/release/
frontend/dist/
backend/dist/

# Logs
*.log
**/*.log

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/

# App local data — user's private data, NEVER commit.
# The entire data dir is runtime-generated and contains the user's résumés,
# cover letters, company/vacancy data, Gmail tokens, and the BYOK API key in
# settings.json. (Previously only some sub-paths were ignored, which leaked
# settings.json + company data into git — see stage/m0 SEC-4.)
app/data/

# Backend
backend/data/

# Temp
**/tmp/
**/*.tmp

# Generated icons (committed source SVG only; PNGs/ICOs regenerated)
# Comment these in once icons are stable to commit them:
# app/build/icon.png
# app/build/icon.ico
# app/build/icon.icns
# app/build/dmg-background.png

# Internal working docs — analysis / audit / plan / staged tasks.
# Local-only: NOT product code, keep out of the published repo.
simplify-docs/
ecosystem-docs/
compare-docs/
launch-docs/

# This monorepo is npm-workspaces (package-lock.json is the source of truth and
# what CI's `npm ci` reads). A stray yarn.lock resolves a different dependency
# graph than CI and release builds — keep it out of the repo.
yarn.lock
**/yarn.lock

# brainstorm mockups (visual companion)
.superpowers/
